{"name":"Black Panther","hex":"#424242","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Black Panther","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of the Black Panther Party, a revolutionary black nationalist and socialist organization active in the United States from 1966 until 1982."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Black_Panther"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black Panther Party","blocks":[{"text":"The Black Panther Party (BPP), formerly the Black Panther Party for Self-Defense, was an American Marxist–Leninist and black power political and militant organization from 1966 to 1982, founded and led by Huey P. Newton and Bobby Seale. Between 1968 and 1971, it was a nationwide organization with chapters in many major cities, and members were active in many prisons and the party had international chapters in the United Kingdom and Algeria. The party first drew attention for openly carrying firearms in Oakland, California while monitoring police activity; resultantly, members were involved in multiple fatal firefights with police. Its earliest goal was to challenge the excessive force and misconduct of the Oakland Police Department that affected the African American community during the civil rights movement. It advocated for decent housing, community control of education and police, exemption from military service for black men during the Vietnam War, and free breakfast for children. The party's dissolution led to various splinter groups and successor organizations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Black_Panther_Party_%28emblem%29.png/330px-Black_Panther_Party_%28emblem%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Panther_Party","wikidata":"Q189150"},{"title":"Black Panther (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Panther is a 2018 American superhero film based on the Marvel Comics character T'Challa / Black Panther. Produced by Marvel Studios and distributed by Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures, it is the 18th film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU). The film was directed by Ryan Coogler from a screenplay he wrote with Joe Robert Cole, and stars Chadwick Boseman as T'Challa / Black Panther alongside Michael B. Jordan, Lupita Nyong'o, Danai Gurira, Martin Freeman, Daniel Kaluuya, Letitia Wright, Winston Duke, Sterling K. Brown, Angela Bassett, Forest Whitaker, and Andy Serkis. In the film, T'Challa is crowned king of the African nation Wakanda following his father's death, but he is soon challenged for the throne by Killmonger (Jordan), who plans to abandon Wakanda's isolationist policies and use the country's resources to begin a global revolution."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d6/Black_Panther_%28film%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Panther_(film)","wikidata":"Q23780734"},{"title":"Black panther","blocks":[{"text":"A black panther is the melanistic colour variant of the leopard and the jaguar. Black panthers of both species have excess black pigments, but their typical rosettes are also present. They have been documented mostly in tropical forests, with black leopards in Africa and Asia, and black jaguars in Central and South America. Melanism is caused by a recessive allele in the leopard, and by a dominant allele in the jaguar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Black_Panther_-_India.jpg/330px-Black_Panther_-_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_panther","wikidata":"Q207963"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Black_Panther_Party_%28emblem%29.png/330px-Black_Panther_Party_%28emblem%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Black_Panther_Party_%28emblem%29.png/330px-Black_Panther_Party_%28emblem%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_Panther_Party_(emblem).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/64/Black-Panther-Party-founders-newton-seale-forte-howard-hutton.jpg/330px-Black-Panther-Party-founders-newton-seale-forte-howard-hutton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/64/Black-Panther-Party-founders-newton-seale-forte-howard-hutton.jpg/330px-Black-Panther-Party-founders-newton-seale-forte-howard-hutton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Original six members of the Black Panther Party (1966):\nTop left to right: Elbert \"Big Man\" Howard, Huey P. Newton (Defense Minister), Sherwin Forte, Bobby Seale (Chairman);\nBottom: Reggie Forte and Little Bobby Hutton (Treasurer).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack-Panther-Party-founders-newton-seale-forte-howard-hutton.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Black_Panther_movement_newspaper_%2824819735771%29.jpg/500px-Black_Panther_movement_newspaper_%2824819735771%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Black_Panther_movement_newspaper_%2824819735771%29.jpg/500px-Black_Panther_movement_newspaper_%2824819735771%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An issue of the Black Panther Party newspaper from July 1970.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_Panther_movement_newspaper_(24819735771).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/NMAAHC-2012_46_20_1001_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-NMAAHC-2012_46_20_1001_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_so